In article <28AUG96.13550198.0011@AACCI.AACC.CC.MD.US>, Scott Kramer <ZSAKSAK@AACCI.AACC.CC.MD.US> writes:

>I moved this source to my
>AIX 3.2.5 system and It compiled and worked fine.  I am at a loss.
>Please forgive me if this is a simple question, but it is annoying.
>
>long *tloc;
>time(tloc);

You're lucky it worked there.  A pointer has to point AT something.
A bare pointer could be pointing anywhere.  On some system it may
be some random place in the virtual address of the process, just
some random place or no place.  Try something like:

long *tloc, clock ;

tloc = &clock ;

time(tloc) ;

Or:

long clock ;

time(&clock) ;

--
Alan Rollow				alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com




