>         Which are the minimum firmware versions to run Digital Unix 4.0 on the
> Alpha Server 1000 and DEC 3000/800 series? In which firmware CD update
> can I found them. And how can I check the current firmware version?

To find your current firmware revision, su to root and type:

uerf | grep Firmware.

To run 4.0 on your AlphaServer 1000, you need version 5.5 available on
the Firmware Update CD Version 3.5.

Assuming the CD is device DKA400, use this command:
> > > b -fl 0,a0 dka400

To run 4.0 on your AlphaStation 3000/800, you need version 6.6 also
available on the Firmware Update CD Version 3.5.

Assuming the CD is device DKA400, use this command:
> > > b -fl 0,80 dka400



