I posted a possible answer to this problem some months ago:

The problem is with the X server, that continues allocating memory
without ever freeing it. You can solve the problem by changing in the
file "/usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers" the line starting with
":0 local /usr/bin/X11/X" to 
":0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -terminate"
and then rebooting the machine. Now, every time you log out, the
X server frees all the memory it has allocated during the session.

Georg Umgiesser

