Sean,

The data may not be gone, but it effectively not accessible,
because the mkfdmn command initialized the metadata for the domain.

I also have a philosophy that I follow with "user data". I tell the
users that I don't back up their stuff, and that they are responsible
to do it, but I always do. That's so I don't have to deal with a lot 
of grief when I screw up and lose some of their stuff. Also, I am
the hero when I get the 

Here's what you should have done:

move the disk from system A to B
# mkdir /<mount point>
# cd /dev
# ./MAKEDEV <disk name>
# cd /etc/fdmns
# mkdir <domain name>
# cd <domain name>
# ln -s /dev/<disk name><partition>    
# showfsets <domain name>
# mount <domain name>#<file set> /<mount point>


Regards,

Steve

