In article <1996Aug26.193210.2088@jax.org>,
Ruth E. Blackburn <reb@informatics.jax.org> wrote:
>I cannot seem to figure out how to use vdump to back up an AdvFS partition
>to a remote tape drive.  I tried piping the data to standard out and then
>using dd on the remote host, but that failed.  Has anyone done this 
>successfully?
>
>Thanks in advance.
>
This answer is from DEC tech support:

sol:    Since rdump does not work on advfs, he has two choices                  
        1. Purchase DECNSR                                                      
                                                                                
        2. Here's an example using /mnt as the fileset to be dumped and         
        nodex as the nodename for the remote node:                              
                                                                                
    # vdump -0f - /mnt | rsh hostA "dd bs=20K of=/dev/nrmt0h"                   
                                                                                
                                                                                
    Then to vrestore it use:                                                    
                                                                                
    # rsh nodex -n dd if=/dev/rmt0h obs=60k | /sbin/vrestore -xf - -D /mnt      
            


