In article <4vsbeb$d3g_001@iroe.fi.cnr.it>, menca@iroe.iroe.fi.cnr.it 
(Dr Francesco Mencaraglia) writes:
|>sorry if this question has been already posed N times ( N >> 1), but I could 
|>not find the answer in the osf FAQ. I am trying to compile a C programs which
|>calls fortran-77 routines.  what I do is:
|>f77 -c routine.f
|>cc -c programc
|>cc program.o routine.o -lUfor -lfor -lm
|>but I get a few unresolved symbols (something like _Ots....); inspecting 
|>/usr/lib I found some libraries libots.a libots2.a but this was not enough.

Use the f77 driver to do the linking.  It will add the proper libraries.
You must also add -nofor_main if the main program is not Fortran.   You can
use the f77 driver to compile the C code as well.  For example:

  f77 -nofor_main routine.f program.c

For further information, please see the Digital Fortran User Manual.
