: there must be a parameter in the /etc/printcap that needs twitching.
: Can someone help with a pointer please? (I tried for myself to get
: access to an OSF machine, but failed, and the target machines have no
: man pages.)

I don't know about the stock LPD on Digital Unix, but I use a LPD 
replacement called PLP that is capable of multiple printers per queue.

It is available from ftp.iona.ie:/pub/plp and it compiles fine on
Digital Unix (also Linux, Ultrix, etc).  Apparently further
development has been discontinued, and there is a package called
LPRng (LPR next generation) that has evolved from it - I believe it
also supports the features you're looking for.

