Here we have already upgraded our machines. We run into problems, of
course, but Digital Unix 4.0 really value all of them (actually while I
am writing I am upgrading our main server :)))

1) The 64/65megs standard root partition is nothing near enought. I was
lucky to have one of the two machines not configured yet, so I could
scratch everything and have a fresh start. Thought the other machine I
had to increase the root partition by taking space from the swap (thank
God the swap is right after the root!). I then restored the original
root and now it is upgrading nicely!

2) The CDE and Digital Unix in general eats more memory than 3.2x. Now I
just had to increase the swap of another machine for that reason.

3) Digital Unix officially support multiple IPs on the same interface.
That means that our problems should (hopefully) be solved once and for
all :)))

Whole in whole it is a DEFINATE impruvment. and by the way, there is
already a patch to install per the 4.0. I still have to install it, but
I belive it is gonna solve several problems that from time to time tend
to come up.

