Hi All,

I'm trying to use rdump to backup an Alpha running Digital UNIX 4.0 to a
tape drive connected to a SPARC running Solaris 2.5.

Unfortunately, rdump is not cooperating:

# rdump -0uf crystal:/dev/rmt/0cn /
rdump: Dumping from host glint.reflections.com.au
rdump: Date of this level 0 dump: Mon Aug 19 16:20:07 1996 EST
rdump: Date of last level 0 dump: the start of the epoch 
rdump: Dumping /dev/rrz3a (/) to /dev/rmt/0cn on host crystal
rdump: Mapping (Pass I) [regular files]
rdump: Mapping (Pass II) [directories]
rdump: Remote system is not known to be compatible for magtape
functions, output being treated as regular file
rdump: Estimate: 43365 tape blocks on disk
The available blocks(14175),is less than the estimated blocks(43365)
Dump is being aborted
rdump: SIGTERM received 
rdump: The ENTIRE dump is aborted


I don't think the error is the fault of the SPARC, because I cannot even
get the Alpha to back itself up to a local file:

# dump -0uf /var/tmp/test.dump /
dump: Dumping from host glint.reflections.com.au
dump: Date of this level 0 dump: Mon Aug 19 16:27:10 1996 EST
dump: Date of last level 0 dump: the start of the epoch 
dump: Dumping /dev/rrz3a (/) to /var/tmp/test.dump
dump: Mapping (Pass I) [regular files]
dump: Mapping (Pass II) [directories]
dump: Estimate: 43369 tape blocks on disk
The available blocks(17765),is less than the estimated blocks(43369)
Dump is being aborted
dump: SIGTERM received 
dump: The ENTIRE dump is aborted

The above error is very suspicious, since there is heaps of free space
in /var/tmp. The 17765 is the amount of free space in /, but /var/tmp is
not in the / filesystem! Also, the rdump (first output above) gave
exactly the same error, with the same sizes and everything...


I cannot even get the Alpha to send the dump output to stdout:

# dump -0uf - / >/dev/null
dump: Dumping from host glint.reflections.com.au
dump: Date of this level 0 dump: Mon Aug 19 16:29:39 1996 EST
dump: Date of last level 0 dump: the start of the epoch 
dump: Dumping /dev/rrz3a (/) to standard output
dump: Mapping (Pass I) [regular files]
dump: Mapping (Pass II) [directories]
dump: Estimate: 43369 tape blocks on disk
The available blocks(0),is less than the estimated blocks(43369)
Dump is being aborted
dump: SIGTERM received 
dump: The ENTIRE dump is aborted


So, any ideas?
I assume DEC did test dump & rdump on DU 4.0...??


