While some of the earlier releases 2.0 or less my have had problems
I've been using Digital Unix 3.2{cd} and 4.0 without problems for
several years.

I'll agree that is a very good platform to start your port from
for numerous reasons.

1) Compilers are strict (and can be made very strict via compiler
   flags)
2) Man pages indicate compliancy of the different system and non-system
   calls.
3) FUSE has a lot of nice features for developing and maintaining
   large projects (RCS, profiler,xref, class browser, graphical
   debugger, + more)
4) ATOM toolkit which allows instrumentation of object level code
   can be used to automatically debug executables.



