I've been working on OSF, now Digital Unix, for quite some time now.
My systems have been very stable - and I beat on them pretty severely
during the course of my work day.

That work day is spent as one of the developers on the Ladebug 
debugger, which comes as part of Digital Unix.  Ladebug takes dbx 
commands, and allows you to attach to a process - so you could
get an interface you're used to with the features you need.

