I don't know what JianLin means when he say "HP-UX doesn't allow you
to attach to a process from a debugger ...". However, I will agree with
him if he means "have trouble to attach". Our company upgradated to 
HP-UX 10 recently and I do get trouble on attaching a running process 
For small test code, there is no problem at all. But when trying to 
attach our real code process(we do vfork()+ *exec()* because we use 
pthread and need to avoid the hassle of thread resource management in 
child process, so, attaching is the easiest way to catch and debug the 
child process), the xdb simply issues "Attach failed":

   %guest: ps -fu guest

     UID   PID  PPID  C    STIME TTY       TIME COMMAND
   guest 16548     1  0 17:42:44 ?         0:00 bin/a.out
    ... 

   %guest: xdb -d src bin/a.out -P 16548
   ....
   Attaching process 16548
   Attach failed
   %guest:

without further message. I am not work with JianLin despite we post 
from same domain(I work in SF Bay and he in Toronto believe me or not). 
So, if he has same trouble (i just know that from his post and your 
followup)on attaching running process with xdb, then xdb must has some 
bugs on attaching process not documented by the man page and the Release 
Notes. Of cause, my code certainly has *lots of* bugs. That is what the
xdb for, isn't it? 

However, I am not trying to say HP is a good or poor system for 
development job(actually, I would like to work on HP for some kind job 
and like to work on other platforms for other kinds of projects). 
Sometime, you would like pick one depend on what you are going to do
(for example, I am now using DCE which is boundled with HP, so I will
not consider solaris or sunos even they are also nice and systems) and 
sometime you simply have no choice.

