Folks,
I had a problem with an advfs file system this morning.
The `df -k' command reported that the file system was full
(7 blocks available out of 1000000) while a `du -s -k' on
it reported only 464825 blocks used.

I have observed the same discrependancy with advfs's
commands:  showfsets (100 % full) and vquot (46 full).

I have checked that no ``known'' process were writing data
on the disk, neither from local processes nor from nfs
clients running elsewhere.

Eventually, I rebooted the system and the ``wasted''
disk space was recovered.  Funny enough, the showfsets
command executed before and after the reboot showed that
the number of files was the same (22043) while the number of
blocks (512b) dropped from 1999986 to 933242 ...

Well, the reboot solved the problem but I would like to know what
happened ...  Thanks, for your help,

Alain
