Sure, when the GUI comes up, select "UNIX Shell".  The installation GUI will
exit.  Then enter 'restart nogui'.

Alternatively, when the system boots, it will get to single user mode and then
you'll see a message saying the system is initializing for the installation.  A
few seconds after this appears, you can enter ctrl-C to exit the installation
and then enter 'restart nogui'.

