Setuid shell scripts are inherently insecure and are a convenient
way for hackers to get root access.  Because of this, I do believe
that there is some kernel parameter in Digital UNIX that prevents
shell scripts from running setuid, and that this parameter is 
turned on by default.

You should try to rewrite your script in C or some other compiled
language which can more safely be made into a setuid program.

-- 
