>it is safe to delete the files in /usr/var/adm/crash? Thsi directory has
>files that take up about 65Megs! We are running OSF1/ V3.2.

The vm* files in /var/adm/crash are sparse files. To find out how
much disk space they really occupy use `du -k'. The files are only
needed for debugging after a crash. Sometimes DEC support asks for
them if you open a call. Normally, it should be sufficient to keep
the crash-data.* files, however.

Hope this helps
Steffen.

