From: tony@linus.newcastle.edu.au (Tony Dyson)
Subject: DU4.0: Caution re Iris Explorer
Date: 1996/08/05
Message-ID: <4u3ik6$8jf@seagoon.newcastle.edu.au>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 172107614
content-type: text/plain; charset=US-ASCII
organization: The University of Newcastle
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


Think twice about installing DU4.0 if you're running Iris Explorer.

Under DU4.0 the explorer package fails with an internal error. At
this stage NAG say that they are not supporting Explorer under DU4.0.

Treat with a large grain of salt any claims that Digital make about DU4.0
being binary compatible with earlier versions of Digital Unix. Packages which
may cause you problems are Gaussian, Samba, the teTeX binaries, gcc, as well
as Explorer. Some aspects of DU4.0 are very attractive, but moving from 3.2
to 4.0 should be considered a migration rather than an upgrade if my experience
is any indication.

