Bill Kemp <bkemp@medusa.cs.mci.com> writes:

>Does anyone out there know what the values for SIGRTMIN and SIGRTMAX
>from signal.h on Digital UNIX v3.2D should be?  Those constants are not
>in the header file but seemingly, POSIX.4 realtime signals are supported
>based on the other things that are present such as the sigevent_t and
>the sigaction struct.

  Digital UNIX versions prior to 4.0 do not fully support POSIX Real-time 
  signals.  Partial support is there, but not everything.

  On DU 4.0, SIGRTMIN is 33 and SIGRTMAX is 48.

