In order to see what's REALLY going on I'd get a TCPDUMP -

$ MULTINET TCPDUMP /HEX/SNAP=1000 /OUTPUT=file.out HOST ip.addr.of.osfbox

(or do the same on the OSF/1 side.)

Let this run while you do the TELNET.  When the TCP connection
breaks, ^C the TCPDUMP.

