I initially made this mistake with our 2100s. I simply plugged a DAT drive
into the external bus at the back. Worked fine until (bizarrely) I upgraded
the Alpha firmware and suddenly my SCSI bus kept resetting and trashing
the disks. Basically if you've got an internal Storage Works rack you can't
use the external SCSI port because that takes you over the 3 meter limit.
My solution was to backup remotely instead... If you've got the money just
stick another PCI SCSI card in and move the external cable to this card.

