Kok Fock Seng (fskok@silicon.net.my) wrote:
: Hi out there :

: 	I need to run multiple WEB server on my DEC OSF1. For example :
: 		www.silicon.net.my  and
: 		www.dec.com.my

: 	One way I can think of to do this is to configure 2 IP addresses
:         on the same machine. How am I going about to do this ?
: 	I tried to use "ifconfig alias" but no respond.

ifconfig is the way to do it.  That is exactly the way to set up virtual 
web servers, by binding two IPs to the same machine.  I have about 60 IPs
bound every time my web server starts up.  The syntax is the following:

/sbin/ifconfig ln0 alias xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx netmask 255.255.255.128

Your netmask and IP will vary.  Then you should be able to ping 
xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx

-mike




