On Friday, August 09, 1996, Kok Fock Seng wrote...
> Hi out there :
> 
> 	I need to run multiple WEB server on my DEC OSF1. For example :
> 		www.silicon.net.my  and
> 		www.dec.com.my
> 
> 	One way I can think of to do this is to configure 2 IP addresses
>         on the same machine. How am I going about to do this ?
> 	I tried to use "ifconfig alias" but no respond.
> 	
> 	Is there any other way for me to run multiple WEB server on the same 
> 	mechine ?

	I had to assign a second address to a DEC 3000-700 running Digital UNIX
4.0.  The setup menu item for Network Configuration did not produce the
proper "ifconfig" parameters when I added the "alias 128.9.14.5" keyword. 
The "ifconfig -a" command displayed the following information:  ln0
128.9.11.3 netmask ffff0000 broadcast 128.9.14.5  <------- notice the
broadcast address!
When I pinged the 128.9.14.5, it actually pinged the broadcast address
which normally is 128.9.255.255 and I got a storm of echoes.  

Although undocumented, the Digital engineer who helped me said the
solution is to use "127.9.14.5 alias" instead the more familiar "alias
127.9.14.5."  I actually added the prior to /etc/rc.config manually the
traditional way and it worked.






