On Monday, August 05, 1996, Sean Siyuan Chen wrote...
> Hi,
> 
> I have an Alpha Station 255 with pre-installed DU3.2D. Recently, I
acquired
> a external 4GB SCSI drive. Now I want to install Windows NT4.0 on the
> system in addition to DU3.2D, so the system will become dual bootable.
> Do I have to get rid off the stuff on the internal drive /dev/rz (800MB)
and
> start from scratch? Could somebody with similar experience give some
> advice?
> 
	The beauty of the Digital Alpha machines is that you can boot from any
device that is seen at the >>> prompt (even over network.)  Only PC-type
Intel machines running NT HAVE TO boot to disk C, or A.  The initial
bootstrap in NT is hardware-dependent. So you can install NT on ANY SCSI
disk without any regard to the contents of any other attached disk. 






