Daniel Hillman (danielh@panbio.com) wrote:
|> I am trying to find a way to display the amount of RAM on a 
|> DEC 3000 without resorting to the boot prom monitor.
|>
|> Anyone know of a shell-available
|> system command that will display amount of
|> RAM on board?
|>

take the following, compile it (cc -o physmem physmem.c), and place the
executable in your path:

#include <stdio.h>
#include <sys/sysinfo.h>

int     status, *int_buff;

main()
{
if( -1 == (status = getsysinfo(GSI_PHYSMEM,&int_buff,sizeof(int_buff),0,0)))
    fprintf(stdout, "error %d getting GSI_PHYSMEM\n", status);
else
    fprintf(stdout, "Physical memory: %d KB\n", (int)int_buff);
}



